Learning-based control algorithms enable robots to acquire new skills and adapt to unforeseen changes by interacting with the real world. However, for unstructured and unpredictable environments, it is impractical to model system dynamics or anticipate all potential hazards. Consequently, there is a critical need for learning-based control methods that can handle unknown dynamics while providing formal safety and performance guarantees.

Formal verification offers a pathway to such guarantees but typically demands a precise dynamic model and a well-defined operational domain—conditions that are often unattainable in unstructured settings. Therefore, this paper introduces a learning-based approach that operates on observed data alone.

